-- check/good: a pair-keyed lookup table, 1 800 rows on ( Int, Int ) plus a
-- wildcard — a 40x45 grid, which is ordinary code (generated, see
-- tests/corpus/README.md).
--
-- A table like this must not be REFUSED at the default budget. A flat path
-- that read one literal COLUMN and no more would send a TUPLE key back
-- to `isUseful`, which specialises the matrix above every row twice over:
-- ~2n squared, 6 587 936 steps here against a default of 5 000 000 —
-- `pattern_budget_exhausted` on a table with nothing wrong with it. The key
-- path unwraps the tuple and hashes the pair, so this costs 10 802 steps
-- (`checker.md` §6.6). The row count puts the unoptimised cost a third over
-- the default, so this fixture fails the moment the key path stops reading a
-- pair.
pub cell : Int, Int -> Int
cell row col =
    case ( row, col ) of
        ( 0, 0 ) ->
            0

        ( 0, 1 ) ->
            1

        ( 0, 2 ) ->
            2

        ( 0, 3 ) ->
            3

        ( 0, 4 ) ->
            4

